    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #366\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nBranch pushed successfully: `bb/relay-215-implementation-audit-fixes-08-23-add-t-thr_4nea8pdjkw`\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #215: the AI gateway structured completion endpoint and client port.\n\n- **`packages/shared/src/aiGatewayClient.ts`** — the neutral `AiGatewayClientPort` contract that `packages/application` depends on exclusively.\n- **`packages/ai-gateway-client`** — HTTP implementation (`createHttpAiGatewayClient`) posting to `http://127.0.0.1:${AI_GATEWAY_PORT}/internal/complete` with bearer-token auth, a 60s timeout, and strict response validation. All failure modes (timeout, non-2xx, invalid JSON, schema mismatch) map to `AiGatewayFailedError` with a safe `{ reason }`, never leaking provider/body details.\n- **`services/semprec-ai-gateway`** — the new gateway HTTP service exposing `POST /internal/complete`: authenticates the internal token before parsing, strictly validates the request body and a bounded Draft 2020-12 JSON Schema (no remote `$ref`, max 64 KiB), runs the existing daily/monthly budget check before invoking the provider, dispatches to a registered structured-completion provider (Anthropic, via raw `fetch` using the tool-forced JSON-schema technique), validates the provider's response against the caller's schema, and writes the standard audit row exactly once per actual provider response. Startup fails hard if `AI_GATEWAY_STRUCTURED_PROVIDER`/`AI_GATEWAY_STRUCTURED_MODEL` are missing or the provider doesn't support native structured output — no silent default.\n- **Migration `0034`** — adds nullable `project_item_id`/`operation` to `ai_gateway_calls`, threaded through `recordTokenGatewayCall` and the route.\n- **`dependency-cruiser` rules** — `packages/application` may only import `@semprec/shared`'s port, never a gateway implementation or SDK; only `semprec-ai-gateway` may depend on a model-provider SDK.\n- **`.env.example` templates** for both `semprec-api` and `semprec-ai-gateway` documenting the shared bootstrap token.\n- **Integration tests** covering auth (401), validation (400), the drift-shaped success path with full audit-row assertions, `invalid_response`/`provider_failed` (502), and `budget_exceeded` (403, no row written, provider never invoked).\n\nVerified against the full backend CI pipeline: build, lint, format:check, check:pi-import-paths, check-migration-numbering, check:boundaries, test:unit (147 passed), test:integration (897 passed), test:e2e (5 passed) — all green.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
